WEBVTT

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.080
Mahoro's gonna go away...

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:09.430
Mahoro's gonna go away...

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.420
Mahoro's gonna go...

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.310
You can't, I won't let you!

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.410
You said you'd never leave, remember?!

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.920
You said we'd always be together! Always!

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:23.000
Didn't you say you'd be the one person who'd never leave me?

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:28.350
Mahoro!

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:29.190
Maho...

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:57.270
And so, I found myself all alone again.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.420
In the first 14 years of my life,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.410
...I learned the meaning of "loneliness" time and time again.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.810
But there are some pains you never get used to no matter how often you experience them.

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:17.110
In the end, my meeting Mahoro just made me more miserable.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:22.950
I thought I would completely seal away the sights and sounds of that time,

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:28.520
...my friends faces, and that precious memory itself.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:35.440
And I decided never to return to Japan. To that town where Mahoro no longer was.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:39.330
"Jils" was it?

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:40.460
Yep.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:42.840
Do you have a lot of contacts around here?

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.830
Nah, I'm just a simple traveling salesman, chief.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:52.290
Of course, I don't mind at all when people underestimate me like that.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:56.340
Barkeep, another milk with no ice.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:57.490
Coming right up.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:01.680
My line of work is pretty flexible.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:08.390
I'll make deals with anyone, Terran or Saint.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:13.000
What do you sell? Women? Weapons?

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.330
Oh, I'm plenty familiar with both.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:18.050
I've even got some Management regulars who...

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:19.990
That organization doesn't exist anymore!

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:22.720
My apologies.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.410
So, chief, what do you want?

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.060
I want you to transport something.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.160
What's the cargo?

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:41.130
The cargo is me.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:46.830
Name your price, and I'll pay it. I want you to get me to Earth in one piece.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.630
Milk, no ice.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.780
You an Earth native, chief?

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.720
Do I look under 20 to you?

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:07.170
Nah, nah, but you don't look like an old man of 80, either.

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:09.810
Welcome.

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.870
Something the matter, chief?

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:35.250
When a man's lived away from his homeland for too long,

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:40.920
...he starts to pine for the littlest things, the most trivial sights.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:44.570
The huge trees on the mountains behind his house as a child.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:49.240
The wind that crosses the hills, making the grass rustle and sway.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.890
Friends that he shared his dreams with.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.780
And the crashing of the waves on the seashore...

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:57.150
The sun as it sinks beneath the horizon...

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:02.760
I want to go back home, no matter what. Back to that blue Earth.

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:05.620
Jils.

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:06.600
Yeah?

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:10.370
If you're a traveling salesman who plies his trade on the colony worlds,

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:12.640
...maybe you've heard the rumors.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:18.490
About a Vesper assassin who doggedly hunts down Management holdouts.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:21.810
He's a demon that's obsessed with death.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.660
I hear that this flesh and blood human volunteered for this dangerous job,

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:31.490
...even though it's typically only done by combat androids.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:38.520
Of course, they say that more than half of his body has been replaced with machinery now.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.510
I can't understand why someone would do that.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.560
It's dangerous.

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:46.960
It's truly dangerous work...

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:51.030
Because it's not something a human should do!

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:53.550
Heave ho...

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:58.040
Hey, Jils.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:06.380
There isn't a hotel in town that'll let in two armed guys dragging a body bag around.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:08.380
Just ditch that thing and let's go.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:12.210
Ditch it? What in the world are you talking about?

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:18.110
It may be scrap now, but this is a genuine, honest-to-goodness combat android.

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:25.190
Bring this little gem to the right people, and we'll have our hotel money!

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:31.680
You went and cut this one up good, too... What a waste.

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:36.870
Still, it'll fetch a good price. The head doesn't have a scratch on it.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:42.360
Only 150 of these Canan-models were built by Management just before they went under.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:44.470
They're a hot item with... Huh?

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:55.310
Now it's honest-to-goodness scrap.

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:03.710
Hey, wait a minute, Master Suguru!

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:06.620
Don't call me "master". It's just Suguru.

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:13.170
Why does the very sight of androids set you off, anyway?

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:16.570
There was that Mephlis-type a while back, right?

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:19.720
There was no call to burn the thing.

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:23.660
It was completely shut down already.

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:26.840
It's their faces.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:29.900
I hate 'em.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:32.650
Of what, combat androids?

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:34.530
Their faces, huh?

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:39.270
Their human expressions and mannerisms...

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:41.540
They bring up memories of the past.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:43.380
Their voices, too.

