00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:50.890
No way, I don't wanna go back to the stupid hotel yet!

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:53.390
We came all the way out here to the edge of the universe,

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:57.520
...so how come there aren't any souvenirs that shout "space" or "SF"?!

00:08:57.700 --> 00:08:59.460
You know, like T-shirts or keychains!

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:05.060
Okay, we'll go back after we take one more look at that oversized planet!

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.480
You're not getting away!

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:11.050
Uh, Suguru?

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:12.760
Cut us some slack!

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:18.330
Ms. Shikijo, it's more than two hours until the next planetrise!

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:19.910
M-Ms. Shikijo!

00:09:20.270 --> 00:09:22.180
The hotel's gonna lock up!

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.590
You're...

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.230
Got it!

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:37.230
Suguru Misato, year 3 class 4, seat number 32!

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:39.890
<b>CORRECT</b>

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:45.230
Sheesh, men sure go downhill once they're past 30...

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:48.400
Are you still in touch with Kawahara and Hamaguchi?

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:53.880
Oh, that reminds me, what about that flat-chested girl who lived at your place?

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:55.240
No, Ms. Shikijo.

00:09:56.170 --> 00:09:59.620
I haven't been back to Earth in more than ten years.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.670
Oh, you don't say...

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:06.350
Still, how come you haven't aged a day in 20 years?

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.150
It's unnatural.

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:14.190
Hey, don't talk about people like they're some kind of monster!

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:18.510
What you see here is the product of backbreaking effort and investment!

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:21.010
And just to be clear, I haven't had plastic surgery.

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:25.220
This is a 100% pure, all-natural body!

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:32.520
Anyway, I'm glad to see that you're looking well.

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:34.110
You, too, ma'am.

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:39.590
Well, I'm these kids' chaperone, so I'd better get going.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:42.730
Junior high schoolers are so pushy these days...

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:45.180
For their class trip, they wanted to go into space.

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:47.260
All right, let's go.

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:48.210
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:48.710
Okay.

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:50.770
Let's meet again.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:52.560
If you're still alive.

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:56.630
You take care, too, Ms. Shikijo. Goodbye.

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:03.210
An old acquaintance of yours?

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:04.410
Yeah.

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:16.960
We always look out at the same moon,

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:21.220
...but today, I sense something out of the ordinary.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:25.920
Something murmuring... Almost sad.

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:29.720
You don't suppose someone else is going to die, do you?

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:33.970
Ryuga, what makes you say that?

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:37.160
I don't sense anything.

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:39.550
Oh, you don't?

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:44.870
I suppose that means my sixth sense still isn't up to snuff.

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:49.120
I just started training with it, so perhaps I was trying too hard.

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:54.190
I see that you've been going back and forth to Earth quite a lot these days.

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:56.630
Is Minawa doing well?

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:01.130
Yes. She's grown up, but everything else about her is the same.

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:04.880
The truth is... it's Sera that's the problem.

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:09.030
Ever since she was stationed on Earth...

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:15.610
Well, now I've learned how to feel jealousy just like everyone else.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.830
Looking at you laughing like this,

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:29.130
...it seems to me that perhaps Terrans and Saint are completely identical.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:31.700
I'm not so sure.

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:36.110
On the contrary, I've come to feel that perhaps it's our differences that are greater.

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:41.200
A Terran's life span is brief beyond comparison to ours.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:43.630
Because of their fleeting life span,

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:48.100
...they have a great strength deep in their hearts that we could never hope to gain.

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:53.930
To me, it looks like a fire burning within them.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:58.310
Yes, that certainly plays a large role.

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:02.400
I've said too much. Please forgive me.

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:05.000
No, that's quite all right.

00:13:05.460 --> 00:13:08.520
I have experienced much the same thing, so I understand.

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:15.320
If you don't mind, there is one other thing I've meant to ask you for quite some time.

00:13:17.390 --> 00:13:22.560
He was still young back then, a Management executive candidate.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:29.960
He who led us out of the Management base after we were shot down and taken prisoner,

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:32.010
...and he escaped with us.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:36.530
Back then, that man, Yuichiro, and I were bound together,

00:13:37.320 --> 00:13:41.190
...and we became the first Saint / Terran couple.

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:44.740
Then, your bloodline has continued in...

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:49.710
Yes, in the son born to our daughter, Yuka.

00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:52.080
In Suguru Misato.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:06.370
There's nothing to worry about, chief.

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:08.800
I'm gonna borrow this for a minute.

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:11.060
I won't burn you or anything.

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:15.340
Yep, I'm just gonna take your head like a human being.

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:17.940
Here goes. Sorry about this.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:18.950
Jils...

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:21.530
Why did you stab me?

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:22.620
Huh?

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:29.150
'Cause there's a bounty on your head, that's why!

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:34.730
Looks like you're so obsessed with work that you weren't paying any attention to yourself.

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:38.210
And... away we go...!

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:41.780
Are you some kinda moron?

00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:43.340
This...

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:46.930
...is how...

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:48.210
...you use these!

00:14:58.200 --> 00:14:59.240
I blew it...

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:02.830
Aw, what the hell?! You're an android, too?!

00:15:03.230 --> 00:15:05.390
Damn it, this pisses me off!

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:08.630
I bet you escaped from a Management research site!

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:10.330
Aw, crap...

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:12.820
The thing about beam saber wounds...

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:15.170
Is that they ain't covered by my insurance!

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:19.600
And of course you don't know that, you dumbass! Hick!

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:21.840
You an Earth native, chief?

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:25.300
Me? Yeah, I'm from Tokyo.

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:28.610
A town called Hiryu out on the outskirts.

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:32.890
You're leaving?

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:37.590
C'mon, finish destroying me!

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:38.870
Forget it.

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:46.880
<i>If you're gonna take a wife, make it a Hiryu girl...</i>

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:49.720
<i>They're beautiful,</i>

00:15:47.970 --> 00:15:49.920
I hate it when this happens...

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:52.000
<i>...sweet...</i>

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:55.160
<i>...and well-behaved...</i>

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.710
Damn, that hurts...

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:02.010
Crap...

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:06.950
I think it went though my natural organs, too...

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:10.040
Still dawn, huh...?

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:14.010
I guess the doctors won't be open yet...

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:21.830
Our next journey will prove to be a long one, won't it, Matthew?

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:26.570
To be honest, it's beyond my imagination, as well.

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:31.810
It's not even clear whether another humanity can exist in the universe.

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:38.050
Please select the absolute minimum number of volunteers to accompany us.

00:16:38.770 --> 00:16:40.950
This will be a journey with no destination.

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:43.960
We are all used to aimless wandering.

00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:48.870
But I've removed those who would look back on Earth with regrets.

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:51.840
It would just be too painful for them.

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:55.730
What of your own memories, Leesha?

00:16:56.490 --> 00:17:01.230
I have chosen my path as a Saint and abandoned my family to come this far.

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:03.190
I have nothing now.

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:04.240
Except?

00:17:05.140 --> 00:17:09.000
Yes, except there is one thing that troubles me.

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:13.260
<b>Cocktails Made with the Latest Machinery! 250 Varieties!</b>

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:13.040
I can't stand cocktails.

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:18.290
And anyway, cocktails and oden noodles don't go together, old man!

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:22.690
If you don't like it, leave your money on the table and get out, you thug.

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:23.430
<b>First Saint Robber Gang Appears: "Saint-like" Theory Crumbles</b>

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:23.430
<b>First Saint Robber Gang Appears: "Saint-like" Theory Crumbles</b>

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:29.000
Oops.

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:31.820
Ow...

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:35.200
What kind of good luck charm is that?

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:39.070
This isn't... a good luck charm.

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:42.600
I just keep it so I won't forget somebody who betrayed me.

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:46.890
It's none of my business, but you're better off letting go of women from your past.

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:50.600
It happened back when I was a kid.

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:53.440
That's a long time to carry a torch for somebody.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:54.610
I SAID, that ain't why I...

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:57.530
Are they good memories?

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:00.180
Yeah...

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:05.620
Back then, every day was bright and sunny.

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:07.790
Everything.

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:11.720
It was like we were standing in the springtime sun all year round.

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:15.240
Everybody has a time in their life like that.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:20.610
The springtime sun, huh... You've got to hold on tight to that.

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:23.050
Geez, make up your mind!

00:18:24.920 --> 00:18:27.300
Shochu diluted with hot water, with a salted plum.

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:29.430
Well I'll be... You DO have real drinks here.

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:31.630
How old are you, old man?

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:33.130
33 this year.

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:37.350
Huh? You're a year younger than me? Man, you look old!

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:39.420
Aw, who asked you?

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:44.130
You don't need to worry about him.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:48.240
Suguru Misato has a very strong spirit.

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:51.790
But he's so very lonely right now...

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:58.490
I have decided today to leave behind a portion of my memory for him.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:02.950
One of your precious memories? Will that be permitted?

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:08.280
Twenty years ago, a region I have never been able to cope with was born...

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:12.930
...within me, Matthew, the collective consciousness of Saint.

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:15.300
The emotion known as nostalgia.

00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:18.640
It is a memory of the springtime sun.

00:19:19.560 --> 00:19:24.990
This memory will be of no use to us on our journey,

00:19:26.050 --> 00:19:28.350
...but I believe it will prove helpful to him.

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:34.690
Where...

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:37.440
...am I?

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:40.820
Suguru...

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:43.830
I need to find Suguru...

00:19:45.630 --> 00:19:46.220
But...

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:49.480
How?

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:55.160
Um...

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:01.930
This ain't good...

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:05.300
I'm breathin' my last, and I'm seeing some weird shit.

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:08.500
The old man at the noodle shop is right.

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:10.060
I gotta get over her.

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:12.720
I've got one weird grim reaper lookin' over my shoulder.

00:20:13.530 --> 00:20:18.470
Um, I'm looking for a junior high school boy who wears glasses.

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:19.900
Have you seen him?

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:31.190
I waited for you all alone...

00:20:32.670 --> 00:20:35.460
I mean, you said you wouldn't go anywhere!

00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:37.660
You said we'd always be together...

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:40.580
Suguru...?

00:20:44.990 --> 00:20:48.800
I got me a cutie reaper here... I must be losing it.

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:52.570
If I go over to 3rd Avenue and get laid, it'll be morning in no time...

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:55.000
If I'm still alive then, I'll go see a doctor...

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:55.930
Suguru.

00:20:57.460 --> 00:20:59.290
Dirty thoughts are bad!

00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:02.170
Let's go back home.

00:21:03.310 --> 00:21:04.990
Back to that town where everyone is waiting.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:10.540
Mahoro...?

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:16.230
Mahoro!

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:17.850
Suguru!

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:21.710
Mahoro!

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:23.490
Suguru!

00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:25.520
I'm sorry, Suguru!

00:21:26.270 --> 00:21:31.840
I... I left you all alone, Suguru!

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:34.910
Mahoro! It IS you, Mahoro!

00:21:35.430 --> 00:21:36.260
Thank goodness!

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:38.360
It's you, Mahoro!

00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:41.750
Thank goodness... Thank goodness...

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:43.740
You're alive!

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:46.980
Thank you so much for being alive...

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:55.240
Mahoro!

00:21:55.820 --> 00:21:57.020
Let's go on a picnic!

00:21:57.130 --> 00:21:59.250
With some tasty boxed lunches!

00:21:59.410 --> 00:22:01.750
I mean, look at how great the weather is!

00:22:05.600 --> 00:22:10.350
まなざしそっとひとつ

00:22:05.600 --> 00:22:10.350
manazashi sotto hitotsu

00:22:05.600 --> 00:22:10.350
Making a single gentle glance

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:11.010
Hey... Hey, wait a minute... Didn't we do this before?

00:22:11.070 --> 00:22:16.120
誰にもみつからぬように

00:22:11.070 --> 00:22:16.120
dare nimo mitsukaranuyouni

00:22:11.070 --> 00:22:16.120
as if no one is watching you,

00:22:11.340 --> 00:22:14.510
Sheesh, what is it with you guys and hiking in the mountains?

00:22:14.650 --> 00:22:18.410
You're wearing high heels again, Ms. Shikijo?

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:26.810
ふんわり時間だけが流れては消えてく

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:26.810
funwari jikan dake ga nagarete ha kieteku

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:26.810
casually, the flow of time dissipates.

00:22:18.930 --> 00:22:21.250
You never learn, do you?

00:22:21.690 --> 00:22:25.000
Hamaji? Huh? Where's Minawa?

00:22:25.120 --> 00:22:28.830
Uh... Minawa? She's over there.

00:22:28.980 --> 00:22:39.290
ねえ きっと願い言葉は空へと届いて

00:22:28.980 --> 00:22:39.290
nee kitto negai kotoba ha sora heto todoite

00:22:28.980 --> 00:22:39.290
Hey, I’m sure the words of desire will reach the sky.

00:22:30.400 --> 00:22:33.060
Hey! Minawa!

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:37.780
Look at how far up she is... She'll never hear you.

00:22:39.100 --> 00:22:42.970
Whew... Here's the summit.

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:52.220
後悔i涙も想い出になるはず

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:52.220
koukai mo namida mo omoide ninaruhazu

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:52.220
Regrets and tears should also become your memories.

00:22:43.780 --> 00:22:44.390
Everybody!

00:22:46.350 --> 00:22:49.820
It looks like I got here too fast...

00:22:50.270 --> 00:22:52.390
Uh... What should I do?

00:22:54.550 --> 00:23:00.690
ならんで歩いたこの道

00:22:54.550 --> 00:23:00.690
narande aruita konomichi

00:22:54.550 --> 00:23:00.690
Walking and following this road,

00:22:55.670 --> 00:22:58.150
Oh, I know! I'll climb down and then come back up again!

00:22:58.550 --> 00:23:02.330
So anyway, what was your dream, Mahoro?

00:23:01.170 --> 00:23:05.500
いつか いつか此処に帰ってくるよ

00:23:01.170 --> 00:23:05.500
itsuka itsuka koko ni kaettekuruyo

00:23:01.170 --> 00:23:05.500
Someday, one day, it will bring me back here

00:23:02.830 --> 00:23:04.250
Hey, that's right, you never told us!

00:23:04.730 --> 00:23:06.170
My dream?

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:18.410
なにげなく振り向いたらほら君の笑顔

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:18.410
nanigenaku furimuitara hora kimi no egao

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:18.410
and I’ll innocently turn my head…making you smile.

00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:07.730
We want to know.

00:23:08.380 --> 00:23:09.710
Well, my dream is...

00:23:10.110 --> 00:23:11.640
Yeah...?

00:23:14.130 --> 00:23:17.100
Oh, I know! It's to become Suguru's wife!

00:23:18.460 --> 00:23:20.930
Suguru, your face is beet red!

00:23:20.990 --> 00:23:23.910
I'm so jealous!

00:23:24.560 --> 00:23:26.960
There's little hope for us in the future, I guess...

00:23:27.120 --> 00:23:28.830
It's a dream. When it's all said and done, it's just a wish, got it?

00:23:28.930 --> 00:23:30.890
Yeah, yeah... It's just a dream.

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:33.750
I came out and said it!
